Hosts Android apps in GameActivity of the AndroidX games libraries instead of NativeActivity. GameActivity is an AppCompatActivity whose SurfaceView lives in an ordinary view hierarchy, so views, fragments, dialogs and the Activity Result API work over the app. GameActivity_onCreate replaces ANativeActivity_onCreate and keeps the render thread, its pipe and its handshakes with the UI thread. Input arrives on the UI thread, which copies it into a locked queue that the render thread drains, hands to native_event_cb and translates: touches, and keys through a key table together with the characters that hardware keyboards type. The UI thread decides at once whether the app takes a key, which it does for translated keys, typed characters and the keys that key_consumed_cb asks for, so back and the system keys go on to the views and the system, and the press of a key decides for its release, so a release whose press went to a view never reaches the app. The visibility of the soft keyboard reaches sapp_keyboard_shown() through the same queue, save_state_cb and sapp_android_get_saved_state() carry the native saved state of the activity across its recreation and the end of its process, and the Choreographer frame loop is chosen at run time, because AChoreographer_postFrameCallback64() exists only from Android 10 on.

